{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And they died before HaShem.</b> Perhaps it alludes to the reason for their death, which was to instill fear so that one would be in awe of the Mishkan upon seeing that those who drew near before Him died. It further alludes that their death was on account of their having preceded [themselves] before HaShem, after the statement of our Sages of blessed memory (Leviticus Rabbah 13:10) that their death was because they had preceded [the verse] ״וַיֶּחֱזוּ אֶת הָאֱלֹהִים״ etc. (Exodus 24:10), and they are the very same nobles of the children of Israel."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:54:48.180547813Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}